Problem Statement – Job Scheduling
The problem is to assign a set of jobs to different time slots based on the machines required to execute them. 
Multiple jobs may be scheduled simultaneously only if they use different machines. 
The goal is to find an optimal schedule that minimizes machine conflicts, ensuring that no two jobs requiring the same machine are assigned to the same time slot.

Parallel Cellular Algorithm (PCA) is used to explore multiple schedules simultaneously and find a schedule with minimum conflicts.
